 methodologies, and explore a series of archaeological case studies, using examples from both the ancient world and the European expansion over the past 600 years. The seminar provides a comparative perspective on indigenous-colonial relationships, in particular exploring the hard-fought spaces of relative autonomy created and sustained by indigenous peoples.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": "(CA-AG, HA-AG)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AG", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2881, "crseId": 354481, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "AIIS", "catalogNbr": "4970", "titleShort": "Independent Study", "titleLong": "Independent Study", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "IND", "ssrComponentLong": "Independent Study", "section": "606", "classNbr": 17536, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "08/26/2024", "endDt": "12/09/2024", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "fwg1", "firstName": "Frederic", "middleName": "Wright", "lastName": "Gleach"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": null, "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": null, "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Students from all Colleges must submit a College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS) Special Studies Form (https://cals.cornell.edu/undergraduate-students/student-services/academic-resources/special-studies-academic-policies-and-petitions-and-forms/undergraduate-special-studies-enrollment-non-structured-credit). Upon approval, students are responsible for enrolling th